  "material": "Actual retained1254 source, canonical512 and decoded256/512 show tangible dense grey stone, coherent mineral grain, pits, chipped facets and ochre weathering. Limestone-like interpretation is plausible; exact geology is not asserted. Detail does not read as abstract grain, pixel contours or an added noise layer.",
  "nativeFidelity": "Two upper faces and one broad lower face retain native colours, course/joint positions, characteristic diagonal chips and feature scale. Both native and decoded replacements at32/16 with BOX preserve representative grey/ochre relationships and intended forms. Natural detail is an interpretation rather than pixel equality.",
  "nativeWrapJointFinding": "Independent original-vs-decoded full-width X roll confirms narrow mortar at native X wrap in the lower course; it is not an introduced seam. Full-width Y native comparison likewise confirms the native horizontal wrap course. Candidate colour, height, XYZ, both textured and neutral opposed lights and literal corners preserve these intended joints without added framing or a disconnected break.",
  "partialFractureFinding": "The lower-left fracture terminates within the lower stone face and leaves a broad stone bridge above it. Direct native/canonical lower-left comparison and full[34,64)lowercourse strips do not show an invented complete little block or full internal mortar division.",
  "physicalDepth": "Source-classified rough stone samples A/B/C remain above central/horizontal mortar D/E after actual tier compression. F boundary/arris, G/H fracture/rim and I/J weathering transitions remain mixed observations, not pure neighborhood proof. Opposed neutral/textured lighting is plausible for worn stone and shows no independent raised ochre coating.",
  "literalExtentClarification": "Author strip code actually uses end-exclusive native[34,63). Independent review extends to[34,64), including bottommost row, and checks fullwidthY[-8,8). Author source/role/labels/fullPNGbytes replay exactly. No small thumbnail or omitted bottom row is used to accept a seam.",
  "diagnosticCorrection": "The generic F witness crop includes out-of-image black padding on its right. It is retained with that limit, excluded from boundary classification, and replaced for actual review by an explicit cyclic F crop. Literal wrap strips never use such padding. This is a diagnostic correction, not an asset failure.",
